Marker: this tree is on the parallel-eval line (vibe-coding/unforce-parallel-*).

Its presence makes eval-stack-parity.sh use the RELAXED "never overflow sooner
than single-threaded base" contract (lower-check teeth kept; upper exact-edge
check relaxed so overflowing LATER than base, frames <= base, is allowed).

This marker lives ONLY on the parallel-eval line and must NOT be copied to the
shipping branch (vibe-coding/unforce). Without it, eval-stack-parity.sh defaults
to STRICT exact-edge parity -- so if the test migrates toward shipping without
this marker it fails SAFE (strict), mechanically enforcing that the relaxed
parallel-line contract never reaches shipping.

STACK_PARITY_EXACT_EDGE=1 forces strict even when this marker is present.

See notes/identity/STACK-PARITY.md ("Parallel-line contract") and
notes/reviews/unforce-parallel-inc2a.md. User-approved (parallel inc2a review).
